# Flutter admin — orders, refunds, and payments (e-commerce)

This plan maps the **Satya backend** e-commerce BRS-aligned APIs to a **Flutter admin app** (admin / superadmin). Base URL example: `https://<host>/api/v1`. All calls use `Authorization: Bearer <Firebase JWT>` unless noted.

---

## 1. Roles and access

- Treat **`admin`** and **`superadmin`** as allowed for every endpoint below that says “admin”.
- If the token role is neither, hide the module or show a locked state.

---

## 2. Core API reference (admin)

### 2.1 Orders

| Action | Method | Path | Notes |
|--------|--------|------|--------|
| List all orders | `GET` | `/orders/all` | Query: `page`, `limit`, `orderStatus` or `status`, `paymentStatus`, `user` (ObjectId), `search` (order number substring) |
| Order detail | `GET` | `/orders/:id` | Same id as Mongo `Order._id` |
| Update fulfilment status | `PATCH` | `/orders/:id/status` | Body: `{ "status": "PROCESSING" \| "SHIPPED" \| "DELIVERED" \| "CANCELLED", "note"?: string }` |
| **Important:** `SHIPPED` requires `tracking.trackingNumber` already set (see §2.2). |
| Update payment fields | `PATCH` | `/orders/:id/payment` | Body: `{ "paymentStatus"?, "paymentMethod"? }` — use sparingly; Paystack flow normally sets PAID via verify |

### 2.2 Tracking and dispatch

| Action | Method | Path | Body |
|--------|--------|------|------|
| Set tracking only | `PATCH` | `/orders/:id/tracking` | `{ "courier": string, "trackingNumber": string, "trackingUrl"?: string }` |
| Set tracking + mark shipped | `POST` | `/orders/:id/dispatch` | Same as tracking + optional `"note"` |

**UX rule:** Prefer a single “Dispatch” screen that calls `POST …/dispatch` after the admin enters courier + AWB. Alternatively, two-step: save tracking with `PATCH …/tracking`, then `PATCH …/status` with `SHIPPED` (backend sends tracking email on SHIPPED).

### 2.3 Admin cancel (paid / pre-ship)

| Action | Method | Path | Body |
|--------|--------|------|------|
| Terminal cancel | `POST` | `/orders/:id/cancel-paid` | `{ "reason"?: string }` |

Allowed only when the order is **not** `SHIPPED`, `DELIVERED`, `FULFILLED`, or `CANCELLED`. Restocks if stock was deducted; sets `paymentStatus` to `REFUNDED` if it was `PAID`.

### 2.4 Payments (canonical Paystack)

| Action | Method | Path | Body / params |
|--------|--------|------|---------------|
| Initialize Paystack | `POST` | `/payments/initialize` | `{ "orderId": "<order _id>", "callbackUrl"?: "<https…>" }` |
| Verify (idempotent) | `GET` | `/payments/verify/:reference` | `reference` from initialize / Paystack redirect |

**Admin note:** Verification is usually triggered by the **customer app** after checkout. The admin screen may show “Payment: PENDING” and a **copy reference** button; support can paste the reference into an internal tool or you can add a small “Verify now” that calls `GET /payments/verify/:reference` with an admin token (backend allows admin verify).

Deprecated but still mounted on orders (optional):  
`POST /orders/:id/payments/paystack/initialize`, `POST /orders/:id/payments/paystack/verify`.

### 2.5 Order requests (cancellations, refunds, replacements)

| Action | Method | Path | Body / query |
|--------|--------|------|----------------|
| List all requests | `GET` | `/orders/requests` | `page`, `limit`, `status`, `type`, `user` |
| Request detail | `GET` | `/orders/requests/:requestId` | — |
| Approve | `POST` | `/orders/requests/:requestId/approve` | `{ "adminNote"?: string }` |
| Reject | `POST` | `/orders/requests/:requestId/reject` | `{ "adminNote"?: string }` |

**Approve behaviour (mirror in UI copy):**

- **CANCELLATION** → runs admin cancel on the order (→ `CANCELLED`, restock, `PAID` → `REFUNDED`). Request status becomes **COMPLETED**.
- **REFUND** → sets order `paymentStatus` to **REFUNDED** only (v1: **no** Paystack API refund; finance settles in Paystack dashboard). Request stays **APPROVED**.
- **REPLACEMENT** → creates a new **PAID** replacement order and links it on the request. Request becomes **COMPLETED**.

After approve/reject, the user receives a **request status email** (best-effort on server).

---

## 3. Suggested Flutter module layout

```
lib/features/admin_orders/
  data/
    orders_api.dart          // GET /orders/all, GET /orders/:id, PATCH status, PATCH payment
    order_dispatch_api.dart  // PATCH tracking, POST dispatch, POST cancel-paid
    order_requests_api.dart  // GET list, GET one, POST approve/reject
    payments_api.dart        // POST initialize, GET verify (if exposed in admin)
  domain/
    order_models.dart        // Order, OrderItem, Tracking, Invoice, Fulfillment, enums
    order_request_models.dart
    order_status_machine.dart // allowed next statuses for buttons
  presentation/
    orders_list_screen.dart
    order_detail_screen.dart
    order_status_actions_sheet.dart
    tracking_form_screen.dart   // or bottom sheet
    dispatch_confirm_dialog.dart
    order_requests_inbox_screen.dart
    order_request_detail_screen.dart
    approve_reject_dialog.dart
```

Use a single **`Dio`** (or `http`) client with interceptors for base URL + bearer token + 401 refresh/logout.

---

## 4. Screen-level UX

### 4.1 Orders inbox (`GET /orders/all`)

- **Filters:** chips or dropdowns for `orderStatus`, `paymentStatus`; optional text field bound to `search`.
- **Row:** order number, customer name/email (if populated), total + currency, payment badge, status badge, created date.
- **Tap** → order detail.

### 4.2 Order detail

**Sections:**

1. **Summary** — `orderNumber`, `totalAmount`, `currency`, `paymentMethod`, `paymentStatus`, `orderStatus`.
2. **Line items** — title, qty, line total (read-only snapshots).
3. **Shipping** — full address from `shippingAddress`.
4. **Tracking** — show `tracking.courier`, `tracking.trackingNumber`, link button if `tracking.trackingUrl`; show `dispatchedAt`, `sharedWithUserAt` if present.
5. **Invoice** — if `invoice.url` present, “Open invoice” (external browser / in-app WebView).
6. **Fulfillment** — `fulfillment.satisfied`, `ratedAt`, `feedback` (read-only; customer-driven).

**Primary actions (contextual):**

- If status allows → **“Mark processing”** → `PATCH /status` `{ "status": "PROCESSING" }`.
- If `PROCESSING` and tracking incomplete → **“Add tracking”** → `PATCH /tracking` then either **“Mark shipped”** (`PATCH /status` `SHIPPED`) or one **“Dispatch”** (`POST /dispatch`).
- If `SHIPPED` → **“Mark delivered”** → `PATCH /status` `{ "status": "DELIVERED" }` (triggers delivery prompt email to customer).
- If eligible for admin cancel → **“Cancel order (admin)”** → confirm dialog → `POST /cancel-paid` with optional reason.
- **Danger:** `PATCH /status` `{ "status": "CANCELLED" }` still exists on the state machine from earlier states — align UI with backend rules (cancel restocks when inventory was reserved).

**Disable rules:**

- Do not show “Mark shipped” until `trackingNumber` is non-empty (or only show “Dispatch” which sets both).
- Hide cancel if status is `SHIPPED` or later (backend will 400).

### 4.3 Requests inbox (`GET /orders/requests`)

- **Tabs or filters:** `PENDING` first (default), then `APPROVED`, `REJECTED`, `COMPLETED`; filter by `type`.
- **Row:** `requestNumber`, `type`, order number (from populated `order`), user, created time, status.
- **Tap** → request detail.

### 4.4 Request detail

- Show **type**, **reason**, **attachments** (thumbnail grid → full screen image).
- Link **“Open order”** → navigate to order detail with `order._id`.
- **Approve** / **Reject** with optional `adminNote` (required for reject in your product policy if you want stricter ops).

**Copy to show before approve:**

- **REFUND:** “Marks order as REFUNDED in Satya. Process the actual refund in Paystack dashboard (v1).”
- **REPLACEMENT:** “Creates a new paid replacement order. Check stock errors — API returns 409-style messaging if stock insufficient.”
- **CANCELLATION:** “Cancels order and restocks. Not allowed if already shipped.”

---

## 5. State machine cheat sheet (admin)

```
PLACED → PROCESSING → SHIPPED → DELIVERED → (customer) → FULFILLED
                ↘ CANCELLED     (admin cancel-paid / status cancel from early states)
```

- Customer **confirm delivery** is `POST /orders/:id/confirm-delivery` (not usually an admin screen); admin only needs to know **FULFILLED** appears after customer satisfaction.
- **REFUNDED** is a **payment** status, not an order status.

---

## 6. Models (minimal Dart fields)

Mirror the backend `Order` payload:

- `String id`, `orderNumber`, `orderStatus`, `paymentStatus`, `paymentMethod`, `totalAmount`, `currency`
- `List<OrderLineItem> items`
- `ShippingAddress shippingAddress`
- `Tracking? tracking` (nullable sub-object)
- `Invoice? invoice` (`number`, `url`, `generatedAt`)
- `Fulfillment? fulfillment` (`satisfied`, `ratedAt`, `feedback`)
- `bool inventoryReserved` (optional display for support)

`OrderRequest`:

- `id`, `requestNumber`, `type`, `status`, `reason`, `attachments`, `adminNote`, `resolvedAt`
- nested `order` (minimal), `replacementOrder` (if REPLACEMENT completed)

Use **`json_serializable`** or **manual `fromJson`** with safe defaults for new nested objects on old documents.

---

## 7. Error handling and ops

- **400 on SHIPPED without tracking:** show inline message: “Enter tracking number first.”
- **409** on replacement if stock fails: show server `message` verbatim.
- **403:** “Admin access required.”
- **404:** treat as deleted or wrong id; pop stack.
- After every mutation, **refresh** order or request detail from GET (avoid stale `paymentStatus`).

---

## 8. Deep links (optional)

If your admin app uses routes, examples:

- `/admin/orders` — list  
- `/admin/orders/:orderId` — detail  
- `/admin/order-requests` — inbox  
- `/admin/order-requests/:requestId` — detail  

Push notifications (FCM) for new orders are **user-facing** in the current backend; admin can rely on **pull-to-refresh** or a periodic poll on the orders list.

---

## 9. Testing checklist (manual QA)

1. List orders with each filter; open detail for PAID + PROCESSING order.  
2. Try `PATCH /status` `SHIPPED` **without** tracking → expect error; then `PATCH /tracking` → success → `SHIPPED` or `POST /dispatch`.  
3. `DELIVERED` from `SHIPPED`; confirm customer receives delivery prompt (email).  
4. Open `GET /orders/requests` with a seeded `PENDING` cancellation; approve → order `CANCELLED`, `REFUNDED`.  
5. Approve **REFUND** on a delivered PAID order → `paymentStatus` becomes `REFUNDED`.  
6. Approve **REPLACEMENT** → new order appears; open it from `replacementOrder` id.  
7. Reject a request with `adminNote` → status `REJECTED`.

---

## 10. Environment (admin build)

- Same **`API_BASE_URL`** as production/staging.
- No extra Flutter env vars required for orders; optional: link template for Paystack dashboard search by `paystackReference`.

---

*End of plan — aligns with backend routes under `/api/v1/orders`, `/api/v1/orders/requests`, and `/api/v1/payments`.*
